RTTipe sizes subranges the way the compiler does.

RTTipe.Get rebuilds a type from its compiled type description; pickles
use it to find where each field is.  It used to size a subrange by
whether its bounds fit in a word of the packing, while the compiler
(SubrangeType.SetRep) picks the smallest of 8, 16, 32 or 64 bits that
holds the bounds, unsigned when the lower bound is at least 0.  So
[0..16_ffffffff] came out 64 bits instead of 32, and with a 32-bit
packing LONGINT subranges wider than 32 bits came out 32.  Each line
compares RTTipe's size of a record field with BITSIZE, under 32- and
64-bit packings.  See LLVM-IR-backend-docs/BUGS.md,
bugs 9, 10 and 24.  Bounds in -255..-64 are left out: the front end
encodes them wrongly (bug 25).
